{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559848-a-comprehensive-guide-to-build-abyssal-entities","id":1559848,"title":"A comprehensive guide to build abyssal entities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-08T20:59:22-07:00","id":1559848,"title":"A comprehensive guide to build abyssal entities","content":"After reading a lot of the core books and browsing a good deal in this forum I find that there isn't a clear way to create abyssal entities. More so, as written abyssal or aren't defined or just use the template of ephemeral entities that makes them lackluster if a mage decide to confront them. Abyssals should be scary and weird, but in a way that doesn't just make them just like horrors or normal sci fi antagonists. For that I propose some rules, mostly stolen from other people ideas, that makes sense to me and maked them easier to build and use in the story.<br /> <br /> First is the nature of the abyss. It has already being said that that is the place that isn't. For that I like to think it like a lower dimesion that the fallen world, like if the fallen word is in the third dimension and the supernal realms in a 4th dimension the abyss should be the two dimensional cracks between them. So, in this line I thought that abyssal entities could be composed by the lack of arcanas, and when they appear in the fallen world they subert the rules of those arcana, trascending it. Mechanically, for each rank a abyssal entity has, it suberts an arcana, in this case I called it nullities.<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of nullities:</b><br /> <b>Time:</b> it exists continuously in all possible times. Can exist inside an ucronia caused or corrupted by it<br /> <b>Fate:</b> it exists outside the realm of possibility. Causality doesn\u2019t affect it and it existence causes paradox<br /> <b>Space:</b> can appear anywhere/exist everywhere at once<br /> <b>Mind:</b> can exist as just an abstract and antieuclidian idea, deforms goetia<br /> <b>Matter:</b> can destroy any substance, seems to be from an illogical substance<br /> <b>Death:</b> is indestructible. Deform or bind souls.<br /> <b>Prime</b>: deforms magic and creates impossible truths.<br /> <b>Forces: </b>deforms or nulls the laws of physics.<br /> <b>Life</b>: deforms and corrupts life, going outside of what is possible.<br /> <b>Spirit: </b>deforms or controls spirits. Can create spirits out of impossible concepts.<br /> <br /> For this I'm working on effects that each nullities grants to the entities, a sort of Numina, with the idea that for each rank the abyssal has it grants it a free &quot;numina&quot; related to that expression.<br /> <br /> This relates to general rules for all abyssal entities making them stronger and more of a challenge for mages:<br /> <br /> <b>General abyssal entity rules</b><br /> <br /> <b>Resistant</b><br /> Entity resist Supernal Magic much more efficiently than other of her kind \u2013 she gets automatic Withstand source equal to its Rank against Awakened spells.<br /> <b>That-Which-Must-Not-Be-Named</b><br /> The ephemeral being can\u2019t be seen by specific mage sights related to ephemeral beings, being registered just as a \u201cvoid\u201d in their senses. However the entity is able to interact with any beings in Twilight and can be affected by abilities that affect beings in Twilight. It still does not count as any 'type' of ephemeral being for purposes of targeting effects, other than being an Abyssal Ephemeral Entity. For purposes of Sympathy casters are considered to not know its name.<br /> <b>Affront to Possibility</b><br /> Sleepers that suffer Breaking Points due to its presence suffer a penalty equal to rank on their roll; on a dramatic fail it can cause a specific abyssal condition and the entity gains essence equals to half the sleeper\u2019s integrity<br /> <b>Abyssal nullity</b><br /> Each abyssal entity represents the lack of a dimension, expressed by the arcana. As such, when manifested in the material realm, they bypass the laws of said arcana. All supernal magic from said arcana results fails if targets directly or indirectly the entity.<br /> <br /> \u200bFinally I like to discuss the distinction between Gulmoth and Acamoths. So far there is a crude idea making the Gulmoths like Spirits and Acamoths like Goetia. I'm using Gulmoths as Abyssal Entities that when manifest have a twillight form or definable expression, while Acamoths like corruptions or infections that exist within fallen beings and only have a concrete manifestation if taken to the Astral Planes.<br /> <br /> I have more to say on this but I would like to hear opinions on this ideas\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28905-keeperofthedarkhound","name":"KeeperoftheDarkHound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28905_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T22:01:11-07:00","id":1559850,"title":"","content":"A lot of the language you are using around this idea presents a particular sticking point.<br /> <br /> There is a part of the Mage setting that is metaphorically buried deeper than the Fallen World, as distant from our world as ours is from the Supernal Realms, broken into many different realms that each lack some element or property that makes up reality. The things from these places sometimes emerge into the Fallen World, where they are inimical by nature because their distinct lack functions like a vacuum, sucking away that property from the world around them.<br /> <br /> <i>It's not the Abyss.</i> It's the Lower Depths. (And, to be really specific, the things that the Lower Depths lack don't map to an entire Arcanum of phenomena, nor fit neatly within a single Arcanum. Examples of things Lower Depths might lack include location, identity, and form.)<br /> <br /> If you think of the Lower Depths in terms of having <i>less</i> of what is real or meaningful, the Abyss is defined as having <i>incompatible</i> reality and meaning. Rather than the empty set, the Abyss is the sum of impossibilities: things that not only <i>don't</i> exist but <i>can't</i> exist, contradictory to the makeup of the world that is. When a piece of the Abyss touches the Fallen World, the result is called a Paradox. Mathematics become inconsistent and hostile. Effects precede causes. Diseases gain consciousness. Memories invert. Things happen that are bizarre and generally forsake and undermine the things the world is built on.<br /> <br /> Your actual ideas, as written, don't necessarily contradict this if you alter the wording. Several of your &quot;nullities&quot; don't actually describe nullities but contradictions. Though again, I think tying it to entire Arcana is overbroad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T18:36:32-07:00","id":1559860,"title":"","content":"The thing is, my idea with this is not so much to develop a new concept for mage but having a way to implement something that already exists, in this case abyssal entities, which are very hard to figure out without falling in something that behaves likes a a spirit or has no rules at all. So far there aren't any entities of the lower depths so I have no need in my campain to develop that. In particular, I completelty eliminated the lower depths from my setting (I eliminated the underwolrd as well since it colided with my conception of stygia). To explain mage cosmology in game, I have a old woman npc moros and baker that shows my players using a supernal cake how it works.<br /> <br /> I'm placing 2 entities as example of where I'm going with this, the second was blatantly stolen from another user<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Monolith</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A large monolithic stone of an unknown material, that shines in the sun with an alien light. The monolith infects the material real around it, making it warp and decay</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Rank 1 Gulmoth</span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Power 4, Finesse 1, Resistance 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Willpower 2 Initiative: 6 Defense: 4 Speed: 0 Size: 8 Health: 4 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Influences:</span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Abandoned places <b>Ban:</b> It can\u2019t enter a brand new place <b>Banes:</b> Orichalcum<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Materialize, Twillight Form <b>Numina:</b> Armored, Compulsion</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Nullities:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Matter</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Matter corruption. </span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Material objects and environment around the entity warp and transform into unnatural elements. The entity can use an instant action to corrupt even living matter in sensory range. If the target is in direct contact with corrupted matter it gains rote in the attack. Resisted by stamina + strength</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Galleroth</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This thing lurks in the cracks of Dissonance created against supernally charged artwork, seeking to draw victims in and trap them in its wrong, twisted galleries that don't exist. It doesn't care to kill--it only wants the awe and reverence artists gain from their work. Whether or not its audience starves in their confused new world is irrelevant. It inhabits the lower floor of an edgy museum, where works of a demented artist are exhibited. Leading to her finding its image in her sketches drawn in that cafe, knowing she never drew that. Sometimes she'll even see those who it has snatched up into its maze. It appears as a figure in a dark coat. His face look like a distorted and abstract representationmade by an artist</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Rank 2 Gulmoth Power: 4 Finesse: 3 Resistance: 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Max Essence: 15 Size: 8 Corpus: 11 Defense: 3 Willpower: 6 Initiative: 6<br /> <b>Influences</b>: Dissonant Art 2 <b>Ban:</b> Cannot force any Sleepers into its maze who are dressed for the occasion in which the art is presented. Cannot manifest physically outside its maze. <b>Bane:</b> Any material that has been used to erase art from a medium it has exercised power over.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Manifestations:</span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Materialize, Twillight Form <b>Numina:</b> Sign, Hallucination, Telepathy</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Nullities:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Time, Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Ucronia</b> <b>(\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, time)</b> Victims who wander into the galleries of Galleroth's corrupted supernal paintings and stare at it a little too long will find themselves unable to leave, transported to a labyrinthic Ucronia of corrupted art. It takes a Wits+Composure check minus Galleroth's resistance to find one's way through to any part of the maze, or to leave it. It can only use this power on a target staring at Supernally enchanted art that has been corrupted by dissonance. Inside people corrupted by Galleroth are trapped.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">That-Which-Must-Not-Be-Seen (Mind)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The ephemeral being is antithetical to the discovery of secrets and powers that reveal information. Such active or deliberate use of powers while the entity in the perception of the user applies Broken, Madness, or Fugue Condition those attempting to use the power. The Condition is considered to be resistant. Roll strength + finesse against composture +resolve</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28905-keeperofthedarkhound","name":"KeeperoftheDarkHound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28905_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T22:46:07-07:00","id":1559862,"title":"","content":"I feel as though &quot;This isn't something new but a way to implement something that already exists&quot; is directly incompatible with things like redefining the difference between acamoth and gulmoth, making Abyssal entities specifically more resistant to Supernal magic as an intrinsic quality, and rewriting their relation to Quiescence and Dissonance, to say nothing of making a topological comparison better suited to its main competition/mutual antagonistic force as Stupid Loserman pointed out above. The 2e corebook compares acamoth and gulmoth to Goetia and spirits as a space-saving measure, but the thematics of the Abyss overall are fairly well-defined this far into Awakening as a gameline.<br /> <br /> The Abyss destroys reason, hope, and being. Its individual manifestations are understandable in a way the infinite Void cannot be, and the dangerous specimens that make their way to the Phenomenal World are sent there to render some facet of ordered reality meaningless by their interface with their surroundings. The Dur-Abzu are the clearest rendering of this, being Abyssal experiences meant to directly negate the messaging of the Supernal Realms, but the cosmological emphases on mockery, ignorance, nonsense, impossibility, degradation and destruction make its place in the Lie clear, at least in its placement as a source of antagonists.<br /> <br /> 2e's emphases are slightly different than 1e, but the classic division between gulmoth and acamoth being their provenance still translates into the current system by the fact that the acamoth's interactions with the world around them were through dreams by which they endeavored to make people's souls more like the Abyss, which has been simplified somewhat from &quot;there's a hibernating thing in the deep Shadow that projects its fever dreams around it and can be convinced to make a deal&quot; to &quot;when the Abyss twists the Astral (which it might do through the proximity of a weird thing in the deep Shadow) it forms acamoth in people's souls.&quot; Not for nothing does Nameless and Accursed's material on the Nasnasi's modified summoning mechanics treat gulmoth as manifest entities and acamoth as recondite.<br /> <br /> Classically the degree of malicious intent and action of an Abyssal being has scaled with Rank, and their contagious unreality is currently represented by the use of Influences to corrupt the phenomena they exist/do-not-exist in mockery of, Abyssal Environmental Tilts spawned by Paradox or other ill fortune, and unique Numina relating to their concept. They're monkey-paw magical potential writ in flesh and effluvia, and while that's infamously got some dire big narrative pops from when things go especially off-course it does require some degree of insidiousness to allow them as a whole to creep into the cracks. They're Mysteries that lead investigators down dead-ends into endless mazes and rabbit holes that terminate in cruel laughter or hollow acceptance. Meddling with Abyssal beings is poking at the force that makes sufficiently overt magic come with a catch, so rather than flatly making magic less effective against them it may be more interesting to tap into Paradox Reach effects and the like \u2014 perhaps an acamoth squatting in one of the ruins of the Spire Perilous responds to spells that use the Mantra Yantra by imposing the Mute Condition on the caster or saps the Finesse of any mage who casts a spell using Runes, or maybe the effects of an Abyssal Verge begin to spread wherever a Gulmoth manifests. (There's also the case to be made that treating gulmoth like spirits leaves the door open for Abyssal fetishes, which in turn serves as an additional avenue for unsettling strangeness.)<br /> <br /> The OP feels like it's describing less that Abyssal beings are particularly difficult to mechanically represent and moreso that the mechanics for Influences and Numina overall are very flexible and pagecount is at a premium for providing examples or intensive suggestions for designing tools to suit a specific concept. These aren't Pangaeans or Idigam or even angels; they don't particularly need extra-strength special mechanics as a consistent feature to be A Problem between having Weird tools in the standard kit and universally treating Paradox, Dissonance, and Quiescence (and Sleepers undergoing breaking points, when Sleepers always suffer breaking points from exposure to Abyssal phenomena) as sources of Essence and healing. An Abyssal entity can primarily be built as a conceptually appropriate Mystery whose core actor is a spirit in name only, breaking out aspects comparable to the powers of Coalesced Idigam from Werewolf for particularly egregious specimens","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T12:23:38-07:00","id":1560072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559848-a-comprehensive-guide-to-build-abyssal-entities?p=1559862#post1559862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These aren't Pangaeans or Idigam or even angels; they don't particularly need extra-strength special mechanics as a consistent feature to be A Problem between having Weird tools in the standard kit and universally treating Paradox, Dissonance, and Quiescence (and Sleepers undergoing breaking points, when Sleepers always suffer breaking points from exposure to Abyssal phenomena) as sources of Essence and healing. An Abyssal entity can primarily be built as a conceptually appropriate Mystery whose core actor is a spirit in name only, breaking out aspects comparable to the powers of Coalesced Idigam from Werewolf for particularly egregious specimens</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the lack of examples of how to build these messy things is an issue.<br /> <br /> I have been meaning to read some of the 1e materials as an example and try to convert for 2e rules... But isn't there an example entity which continues to exist if any individual knows a out it? Or which exist as parallel timelines where they Abyssal timeline just wants to exist in the main world?<br /> <br /> I don't know how I would build that with the mechanical tools you are describing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T16:52:51-07:00","id":1560080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559848-a-comprehensive-guide-to-build-abyssal-entities?p=1560072#post1560072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the lack of examples of how to build these messy things is an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to wordcount. I still don't feel that the denizens of the endless Abyss of malformed creation benefit from having consistent mechanically-enforced oddities beyond those described in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Things from Night Horrors books can get away with having dozens of bespoke examples with unique traits because that's the function of that subline, but if you have a weird quality of an Abyssal being you have that one weird quality and it probably doesn't laterally transfer to other Abyssal beings without some reworking or that transfer being a diegetic plot point, and this is not a situation unique to Abyssal beings; there's a reason Numina and Dread Powers have such a breadth of examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have been meaning to read some of the 1e materials as an example and try to convert for 2e rules... But isn't there an example entity which continues to exist if any individual knows a out it? </div> </div> </div>That is either a Goetia-adjacent thing or a quality that is outside the scope of generalized mechanics to deal with. The Geryo supposedly have this quality and the nature of testing it is such that it is basically impossible to verify without building in an exception that would be just as arbitrary if divorced from the thematic purpose it serves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or which exist as parallel timelines where they Abyssal timeline just wants to exist in the main world? </div> </div> </div>That's a godlike being. Of all the things in Chronicles that are mechanically handled as plot devices, the likes of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves is one of the plot-deviceyest.<br /> <br /> Even if you're somehow talking about parallel timelines as beings of a low enough Rank to have stats, we have a wide variety of cases throughout the Chronicles of Darkness where the ephemeral being systems are used to model places and forces of destiny. Affecting the Corpus of the thing maintaining an unclean dimensional rift may involve more than swinging Ephemeral Enchantment at it, but &quot;this thing can be thwarted piecemeal or in it entirety with the right configuration of reality&quot; is a durable function of the Ban and Bane systems, among other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know how I would build that with the mechanical tools you are describing... </div> </div> </div>The incredibly broadly-defined systems for ephemeral beings are not going to help you wit this, because it is not the role of Chronicles' mechanical systems to tell you <i>how to come up with a spooky weird thing that defies the systems of ordered reality as we know it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T03:45:57-07:00","id":1560088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559848-a-comprehensive-guide-to-build-abyssal-entities?p=1560080#post1560080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The incredibly broadly-defined systems for ephemeral beings are not going to help you wit this, because it is not the role of Chronicles' mechanical systems to tell you <i>how to come up with a spooky weird thing that defies the systems of ordered reality as we know it.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/9407-hunting-down-100-000-leaves#post11974\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/9407-hunting-down-100-000-leaves#post11974\"> Hunting down 100,000 Leaves - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/9407-hunting-down-100-000-leaves#post11974\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/9407-hunting-down-100-000-leaves#post11974 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been running a Mage campaign for about a year and a half now, and my cabal, after months of dealing with scelesti and mad cultists, is on the cusp of attempting to deal with the Prince of 100,000 Leaves' alternate universe (as detailed in Boston Unveiled) by going to an Abyssal echo of it directly. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thank you, I think about of googlong lead me to this thread, and yeah. Annunkai were not on my list of things to &quot;simply model&quot; with the Ephemeral Entity system.<br /> <br /> Or any other system. But nice to know that is a rank 8 entiti, and terrifying...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}